2026-01-19 21:45:21 | INFO | Q165 id=BV1ps4y1w7Wr_00-00-00_00-00-10 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=To estimate the depth of the well based on the sound heard when a stone is thrown, we need to consider the speed of sound in air and the time it takes for the sound to travel down to the bottom of the well and back up.\n\n1. **Speed of Sound in Air**: The speed of sound in air is approximately 343 meters per second (m/s).\n\n2. **Time Calculation**: The time it takes for the sound to travel down to the bottom of the well and back up is given as 1 second. This time includes the round trip, so the time for the sound to travel down to the bottom of the well is half of this time, which is 0.5 seconds.\n\n3. **Distance Calculation**: The distance the sound travels in 0.5 seconds can be calculated using the formula:\n   \[\n   \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time}\n   \]\n   Substituting the values:\n   \[\n   \text{Distance} = 343 \, \text{m/s} \times 0.5 \, \text{s} = 171.5 \, \text{meters}\n   \]\n\n4. **Comparison with Choices**: The calculated distance of 171.5 meters is closest to the range of 100-200 meters.\n\nTherefore, the best answer is:\nB
